# Automated Functional Testing of SauceDemo using Cypress

End-to-end test automation project for the Software Testing course.
The tests run on [SauceDemo](https://www.saucedemo.com), a public demo e-commerce site.

## Tool

- **Cypress** (JavaScript end-to-end testing framework)
- Browser: Electron
- Editor: VS Code

## Project structure

```
.
├── cypress
│   └── e2e
│       └── saucedemo.cy.js   # 8 test cases
├── cypress.config.js         # Cypress settings
├── package.json
└── README.md
```

## Test cases

| ID | Test case | Expected result |
|----|-----------|-----------------|
| TC01 | Valid login | Inventory page opens |
| TC02 | Invalid password | Error message shown |
| TC03 | Locked-out user | Locked message shown |
| TC04 | Sort products by price | Low to high order |
| TC05 | Add item to cart | Cart badge shows 1 |
| TC06 | Remove item from cart | Cart is empty |
| TC07 | Checkout with empty form | Validation error |
| TC08 | Complete checkout | Order confirmation |

## Setup

1. Install [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) (LTS version).
2. Clone this repository:
   ```
   git clone https://github.com/lutfan12haider/cypress-saucedemo-testing.git
   cd cypress-saucedemo-testing
   ```
3. Install dependencies:
   ```
   npm install
   ```

## Run the tests

Visual runner:

```
npx cypress open --browser electron
```

Choose **E2E Testing**, then click `saucedemo.cy.js`.

Headless run (saves video and screenshots):

```
npx cypress run --browser electron
```

## Results

| Total | Passed | Failed | Skipped | Run time |
|-------|--------|--------|---------|----------|
| 8       | 8      | 0       | 0    | 9 seconds |



